  "notes": "Four-camera headless PTP external-IPC run for the detect-latency lever A/B (docs/detect_latency_review_2026_09_03.md). Analyse with scripts/analyze_yolo_latency_phases.py. Levers 1, 3, 4 plus lever 2b: the external handoff waits for YOLO completion before giving the frame to the recorder, so the detach and NVENC input copies run in the idle part of the frame period. Plus lever 2c: registered-source external recorder (NV12-shaped pool buffers registered with NVENC, zero copy, deferred release after NVENC unmap). Plus crop production and crop video with a synthetic centre-box detection on every frame (pose_worker noop, roi_source synthetic_center_box, 384 px box), so the crop is actually cut from the frame and encoded even with no animal in view. The _crop spec without synthetic detections encodes blank crops when the scene is empty. Crop video through the EXTERNAL crop recorder (fixed.crop_recording mode=external_ipc): one supervised recorder process per camera on the other die of its card, so the crop NVENC leaves the detect die. Crop recorders as separate processes on the DETECT die itself (recorder_gpus 2010093->3, 2010094->1, 2010095->7). Pre-test for GOP-parity crop interleaving: if the p99 penalty appears only during same-die GOPs (detect die NVENC busy), routing crops to the idle die by parity recovers it; if it appears in other-die GOPs too, the cost is the extra NVENC session, not the switch.",
